  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Evidence proves GSearch makes no attempt to ensure XML validity before passing the XML to SOLR's update service.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Invalid XML errors are completely lost and obscured in the current implementation; GSearch's log reports an ambiguous \"connection error\" instead of revealing the true source of the error (invalid XML).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "One must manually feed XML to SOLR's update service to reveal the source of the error like so:",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "curl -k --request POST -H \"Content-Type: text/xml\" --data-binary \"@invalid.xml\" ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://localhost:8443/solr/update"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://localhost:8443/solr/update",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<response>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "<lst name=\"responseHeader\"><int name=\"status\">400</int><int name=\"QTime\">4</int></lst><lst name=\"error\"><str name=\"msg\">Illegal character ((CTRL-CHAR, code 27))",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "at [row,col {unknown-source}]: [135,47]</str><int name=\"code\">400</int></lst>",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "</response>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "In the case of the attached invalid.xml, there is an invisible control character rendering the XML invalid.  Attached is also a screenshot showing xmlstarlet's validator result.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Is is my professional opinion that invalid XML should never be passed blindingly to SOLR's update service.   Recommend running GSearch/Apache Tika generated XML through a validator subroutine prior to being passed to SOLR's update service.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Additionally, proper invalid XML error handling, including logging and related error messaging should be wholly reflected in GSearch's log files.  Today's error messaging is misnomer reflecting a communications error.  In reality, it is not a communications error at all, unless one stretches the definition of communications out like taffy to apply to invalid XML.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
